L000517	Figure~\ref{fig:SummaryPlot} compares our observed upper limits with those obtained with several instruments and from observations of different regions of the sky. Our analysis significantly improves the previous constraints on the line cross section from 300 GeV up to $\sim 30$ TeV. Large photon statistics from longer observation time and optimized pointing positions, the exploitation of the full H.E.S.S. five-telescope array, and the application of run-wise simulations for the IRFs~\cite{Holler:2020duc} drive the sensitivity improvement. For a 1 TeV DM mass, the limit is improved by a factor of $\sim 2.1$ with respect to the previous H.E.S.S. results. The constraints obtained in this work are the strongest so far in probing multi-TeV DM models. More details are provided in Ref.~\cite{supplement_more_details}.
